    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0745" n="708" xml:id="pg708"/>

                <head>290. Telegram From the Station in Iran to the Central Intelligence
                        Agency<anchor n="1" xml:id="d290-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                    <placeName>Tehran</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1953-08-20T18:53:00+00:00">August 20, 1953, 1853Z</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    TEHE 756. Re: DIR 16355.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d290-f2"/> Some difference of opinion exists among Iranian officials
                    on best timing for Shah’s return and we think this question best resolved
                    without our involvement particularly since direct communications between Shah
                    and his people now easy. Therefore tell Shah all news most encouraging and we
                    understand his govt in touch with him
                        directly.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d290-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>End of message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency. Secret; Operational Immediate. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] Transcribed specifically for
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi> series from microfilm in the
                    Central Intelligence Agency that no longer exists. See “Sources” chapter.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f2" n="2" xml:id="d290-f2-content">
                <p>Not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f3" n="3" xml:id="d290-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram TEHE 749, sent earlier on August
                    20, the Station requested to “have the Shah start Tehe immediately.” (Central
                    Intelligence Agency. Transcribed specifically for the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Relations</hi> series from microfilm in the Central Intelligence
                    Agency that no longer exists. See “Sources” chapter.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
